# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @nuvem/keeper — configuration
#
# The keeper is the ONLY service in this repo that holds signing keys. Treat this
# file as documentation, never as a place to put a real key: copy it, fill the
# copy, and keep the copy out of git (.gitignore already covers .env*).
#
# NOTHING HERE IS READ AT BUILD TIME. Everything is read at process start, so one
# image runs unchanged locally, on a VPS and on Railway; changing the RPC endpoint
# is a restart, not a rebuild. A key must NEVER be passed as a Docker build ARG —
# build args are visible in image history forever.
#
# DRY RUN IS THE DEFAULT. Running the keeper with no flags performs a dry run and
# cannot do anything else: outside live mode the process never even reads a key
# capable of sending a transaction. See NUVEM_KEEPER_ALLOW_BROADCAST below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- REQUIRED ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Robinhood Chain (chainId 4663) JSON-RPC endpoint.
#   aliases: NUVEM_KEEPER_RPC_URL, MAINNET_RPC, RPC_URL
#
# It must be an ARCHIVE endpoint and it must support debug_traceTransaction with
# the callTracer. Both are load-bearing, not nice-to-have:
#   * archive, because cashStart/cashEnd and every position balance are read at
#     historical block tags. A pruning node answers those from latest state or
#     errors, and the first of those is silently wrong.
#   * callTracer, because it is the ONLY source of sell proceeds on this chain —
#     the GMGN router unwraps WETH and forwards native ETH by internal call, with
#     no log and no top-level transaction. Without it every sell reads as a
#     giveaway and every window refuses.
#
# The URL is treated as a secret: it usually carries an API key, and viem
# annotates transport errors with the endpoint it called. Only the HOST is ever
# logged. Beware that the repo .env has RH_TESTNET_RPC_URL, which is a TESTNET
# endpoint and is NOT this variable.
NUVEM_RPC_URL=

# The trading account. This address IS the settler: SettlementExecutor resolves
# the vault via factory.activeVaultOf(msg.sender), so only the trading account
# itself can submit a settlement.
#   aliases: NUVEM_TRADING_ACCOUNT, or --account 0x… on the command line
#
# NOT the vault admin. On the canary deployment the vault admin is
# 0xaED788B3C69CA941A4302899f80cCAD219942CA7 and activeVaultOf() returns the ZERO
# address for it, so it can never settle. The trading account is a different
# address entirely.
NUVEM_KEEPER_ACCOUNT=

# The attester signing key. PREFER THE FILE FORM: an environment variable is
# visible in /proc/<pid>/environ, in `docker inspect`, and to every child process.
# Mount a 0400 file (a docker secret, or a bind mount) and point at it.
# The variable form is read once and then deleted from process.env.
NUVEM_ATTESTER_KEY_FILE=
# NUVEM_ATTESTER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- THE BROADCAST GATE ------------------------------------------------------

# Broadcasting requires BOTH `--broadcast` on the command line AND this variable
# set to the exact literal string below. It is compared BYTE FOR BYTE — a
# truthiness check would be satisfied by "0", "false" and "no", all of which a
# human writes when they mean the opposite, and surrounding whitespace does not
# count either. Leave it unset and the keeper is a read-only observer.
#
#   NUVEM_KEEPER_ALLOW_BROADCAST=i-understand-this-moves-real-funds
NUVEM_KEEPER_ALLOW_BROADCAST=

# The trading account's own private key. READ ONLY IN LIVE MODE — in a dry run
# this is never touched, which is the mechanical half of "dry run by default".
#
# v1 DELIBERATELY SERVES THE OPERATOR'S OWN WALLET. Holding this key is TOTAL
# custody of that wallet: it can move every token, trade, and revoke the
# EIP-7702 delegation. That is honest for a single-user service where the wallet
# belongs to the operator, and it is exactly why multi-user is not yet possible —
# holding a third party's trading key would be custody of their whole wallet.
# See README.md "The upgrade path" for what replaces it.
#   aliases: TRADING_OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY, NUVEM_TRADING_OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY
NUVEM_TRADING_KEY_FILE=
# TRADING_OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- STATE -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the journal, the snapshot, the instance pin and the writer lock live.
# In a container this should be the ONLY writable mount, and the container itself
# should run read_only with a tmpfs /tmp.
#
# The directory is PINNED to (chainId, factory, executor, vault, account) on
# first use. Reusing a directory created for another deployment refuses to start
# rather than migrating: a volume that once held testnet state is the cheapest
# possible route to a wrong settlement.
NUVEM_KEEPER_STATE_DIR=.keeper-state

# First L2 block the watcher will ever look at. SET THIS near the current head on
# a cold start. The keeper refuses a discovery scan wider than
# NUVEM_KEEPER_MAX_TICK_SCAN_SPAN_BLOCKS rather than scanning part of the range,
# so leaving it at 0 on a chain 23 million blocks tall just refuses every tick.
NUVEM_KEEPER_FROM_BLOCK=0

# First L2 block SettlementExecuted logs are searched from during recovery.
# Public endpoints commonly cap the eth_getLogs range; keep this near the vault's
# deployment era rather than at genesis.
#   aliases: NUVEM_LOGS_FROM_BLOCK
NUVEM_KEEPER_LOGS_FROM_BLOCK=0

# --- ADDRESSES (default to the mainnet canary deployment) --------------------
# The keeper reads the live chain and refuses to act on a mismatch; these are the
# expectation it checks against, not a source of truth.
NUVEM_CHAIN_ID=4663
NUVEM_VAULT_FACTORY=0xDf411fdCc7C31e4F6bCa6F6BCaB40FE812Ab4A46
NUVEM_SETTLEMENT_EXECUTOR=0xCe676c73bd9fb76a73058EC135106b81A5ABd0f5
NUVEM_KEEPER_VAULT=0xF7309dC8e1914A5c3848250cec54Ebe7A20D8255
NUVEM_PAUSE_CONTROLLER=0x2dbbc211dbfe0f15e88e5388c96530f2721baefc
NUVEM_ATTESTER_REGISTRY=0x2a3309931a6db1e1b253224551912566d647f921
NUVEM_WETH=0x0bd7d308f8e1639fab988df18a8011f41eacad73

# --- TIMING ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Poll interval, milliseconds. Default 30000. Sizing: the canary's 258 L2 blocks
# spanned 3 L1 blocks, i.e. ~7 L2 blocks/second, so 30s is ~210 L2 blocks — far
# less latency than the L1 coarseness a settlement has to wait out anyway.
NUVEM_KEEPER_POLL_MS=30000

# L2 blocks left untouched at the head. Nothing inside the margin is detected,
# verified or anchored, so a sequencer reorg cannot move a boundary the keeper has
# already committed to. Cheap here, so lean high rather than low. Default 64.
NUVEM_KEEPER_FINALITY_MARGIN_L2=64

# L1 blocks that must have passed beyond endBlockL1 before signing. The contract
# requires endBlock < block.number in L1 space and L1 advances only every ~12s, so
# a freshly closed session is briefly unsettleable. Default 2.
NUVEM_KEEPER_L1_MARGIN=2

# --- LIMITS, ALL FAIL-CLOSED -------------------------------------------------

# Widest session span the dense verifier may be pointed at. The dense scan is
# O(span) in eth_getBlockByNumber. A wider session is recorded SPAN_TOO_WIDE and
# reported — never split, because a sub-window is not flat-to-flat and would
# refuse anyway, and a keeper that invents its own boundaries is a keeper that
# invents its own profit. Default 20000.
NUVEM_KEEPER_MAX_VERIFY_SPAN_BLOCKS=20000

# Widest DISCOVERY scan one tick may perform. Exceeding it abandons the tick with
# NO verdict. A truncated scan is worse than a slow one because it answers from
# less evidence while looking exactly like a full answer.
#
# Default 2000, sized from measurement: the engine's block scan issues one
# sequential eth_getBlockByNumber per block, which ran at ~21 blocks/second
# against the mainnet endpoint, so 2000 blocks is ~95 seconds. The chain produces
# ~7 L2 blocks/second, so 2000 blocks is also ~5 minutes of real time — more than
# one 30-second poll, which is what a tick has to keep up with. Raising it trades a
# longer worst-case tick for a longer outage the keeper can absorb unattended.
NUVEM_KEEPER_MAX_TICK_SCAN_SPAN_BLOCKS=2000

# Hard ceiling on RPC calls per tick. Budget exhaustion must be indistinguishable
# in effect from "did not look". Default 5000.
NUVEM_KEEPER_MAX_RPC_CALLS_PER_TICK=5000

# Circuit breaker: refuse any single contribution above this, in WEI, and halt.
# This is the OPERATOR's ceiling, independent of the vault's maxPerSettlementWei —
# which the vault admin could raise by mistake. Default 1e15 (0.001 ETH), which is
# the canary vault's own per-settlement cap.
NUVEM_KEEPER_MAX_CONTRIBUTION_WEI=1000000000000000

# Circuit breaker: refuse more than this many settlements in a rolling 24h, and
# halt. Default 8.
NUVEM_KEEPER_MAX_SETTLEMENTS_PER_DAY=8

# Multiple of (gasLimit * maxFeePerGas) that must be spare BEYOND the contribution
# and beyond tradingFloorWei + gasReserveWei. This guards a real hazard:
# previewContribution clamps against the balance NOW, while settle clamps against
# `msg.sender.balance + msg.value` AFTER gas has been debited. If that difference
# makes the clamp bind, the recomputed amount no longer equals the signed
# contribution and settle reverts InvalidContribution — which looks like a
# mysterious signature failure rather than a funding problem. Default 2.
NUVEM_KEEPER_GAS_HEADROOM=2

# --- THE HEARTBEAT SURFACE ---------------------------------------------------

# Bind address for GET /health and GET /status. Both unset (or the port set to 0)
# means no HTTP surface at all, which is right for a one-shot `tick` on a laptop.
# The container image sets both.
#
# DO NOT PUBLISH THIS PORT. /status describes a service holding a signing key.
# Reach it from a sibling container on the compose network, or with
# `docker compose exec`.
#
# The split matters: /health makes NO RPC call and touches no file, and fails only
# when the tick loop is wedged — the one condition a restart fixes. Being
# degraded, dry-run, or unable to reach the RPC does NOT fail it, because a halted
# keeper has to stay up to explain itself and restarting has never once fixed an
# upstream RPC. Never point a HEALTHCHECK at /status.
NUVEM_KEEPER_HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
NUVEM_KEEPER_HTTP_PORT=

# --- OPTIONAL ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Stamped onto every log line so a decision can be tied to a build.
#   aliases: GIT_SHA, RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA
NUVEM_KEEPER_GIT_SHA=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT
#
# No override for a REFUSED window, in any form. There is no
# NUVEM_KEEPER_FORCE, no --yes, no ALLOW_REFUSED. A window the engine cannot
# vouch for is not settled, full stop; that stance is inherited from
# packages/aa-smoke-old/scripts/settle.mjs and it is the point of the engine
# existing. If refusals are rising, the fix is in the classifier or in the
# window, never here.
#
# No session key or bundler configuration. The ERC-4337 / direct-call session-key
# paths are documented in README.md as the upgrade path and are NOT built: neither
# has ever been installed on chain 4663, and the negative tests that would make
# either trustworthy do not exist yet.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
